  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.485–0.650) while image-only with ResNet50 is very weak (0.208). Within RNA, multiprofile+avgpool is the best profile/aggregation combo, and scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 by ~6% (0.650 vs 0.591) under identical settings. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested the third RNA encoder (scGPT) under the same favorable conditions, so we do not know whether scGPT could surpass scvi_n200 or whether scvi_n200 is already near the encoder ceiling. Question tested: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scGPT, avgpool) isolates the encoder variable while holding profile and aggregation fixed, giving a direct scGPT-vs-scvi_n200 comparison. Why best next: The RNA encoder is the highest-leverage design choice given RNA's dominance; resolving it before investing in multimodal or image-encoder experiments prevents committing budget to a suboptimal base representation. A clean single-variable comparison also yields the most interpretable evidence for all downstream fusion decisions."
}

